      "message": "docs(process): a fork syncs from upstream at each cut tag, not continuously\n\nAGENTS.md Issue Law: in a fork (an `upstream` remote exists), fetch\nupstream's tags and fast-forward the fork's main to the newest vX.Y.0 cut\ntag it lacks - never to upstream/main, which changes constantly - then\nbranch issue work from that main. Upstream conflicts are merged into the\nissue branch only; the fork's main moves at the next cut tag. The\ncanonical repo (no upstream) keeps 'Start from the latest main'.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
